WEBVTT

00:00:00.362 --> 00:00:02.290
Last video ended with this question.

00:00:02.954 --> 00:00:05.730
Here's sine x, and sine two x.

00:00:06.415 --> 00:00:08.701
At the origin, sine x has slope one,

00:00:08.943 --> 00:00:10.566
because cos zero is one.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:13.862
Sine two x leaves the origin twice as

00:00:13.903 --> 00:00:15.390
steeply, with slope two.

00:00:16.074 --> 00:00:17.401
Where does that two come from?

00:00:18.207 --> 00:00:20.232
And what happens when the inside part isn't

00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:22.779
two x, but something like x squared?

00:00:23.458 --> 00:00:24.672
You've met the reason before.

00:00:25.397 --> 00:00:28.264
Sine two x is the sine curve squashed

00:00:28.426 --> 00:00:29.588
sideways by a half,

00:00:30.171 --> 00:00:33.058
so every slope, at matching points, doubles.

00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:35.589
The chain rule from Year 11 says the

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:36.030
same thing.

00:00:36.754 --> 00:00:39.402
Two x is the inside part, the expression

00:00:39.543 --> 00:00:41.951
sine is applied to, and sine is the

00:00:42.112 --> 00:00:42.512
outside.

00:00:43.196 --> 00:00:45.541
Differentiate the outside, and keep the inside as

00:00:45.842 --> 00:00:47.486
it is: cos two x.

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:51.064
Then multiply by the inside part's derivative, which

00:00:51.146 --> 00:00:51.547
is two.

00:00:52.192 --> 00:00:54.742
So the derivative is two cos two x,

00:00:55.346 --> 00:00:56.751
and at zero, that's two.

00:00:57.281 --> 00:00:58.667
Now a harder inside:

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:01.600
y equals sine of x squared.

00:01:02.204 --> 00:01:03.540
No squash makes that curve.

00:01:04.386 --> 00:01:07.037
If you only differentiated the outside, you'd get

00:01:07.258 --> 00:01:08.624
cos of x squared.

00:01:09.248 --> 00:01:10.562
Test it against the real slopes.

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:14.034
At x equals a half, both are about

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:16.259
point nine seven, a ratio of one.

00:01:17.062 --> 00:01:19.087
At x equals one, the real slope is

00:01:19.128 --> 00:01:20.572
about one point zero eight,

00:01:21.075 --> 00:01:23.321
but cos of one is only point five

00:01:23.423 --> 00:01:23.702
four.

00:01:24.266 --> 00:01:25.210
That's a ratio of two.

00:01:26.036 --> 00:01:27.702
At one and a half, the ratio is

00:01:27.824 --> 00:01:28.104
three.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:30.463
The missing factor isn't fixed.

00:01:31.087 --> 00:01:33.954
It's two x, the derivative of the inside

00:01:34.016 --> 00:01:35.218
part, x squared.

00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:36.879
Why multiply?

00:01:37.705 --> 00:01:40.100
Follow a small step at x equals one.

00:01:40.805 --> 00:01:42.539
Move x by point zero one.

00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:46.031
The inside, x squared, moves about twice as

00:01:46.092 --> 00:01:48.759
far, about point zero two, because its rate

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.545
there is two x, which is two.

00:01:51.308 --> 00:01:53.677
Then sine reacts to its own input at

00:01:53.717 --> 00:01:56.226
a rate of cos one, about point five

00:01:56.287 --> 00:01:56.547
four.

00:01:57.271 --> 00:01:59.856
So y moves about point five four times

00:01:59.957 --> 00:02:02.362
point zero two, which is about point zero

00:02:02.503 --> 00:02:02.923
one one.

00:02:03.626 --> 00:02:05.127
That's why it's called a chain:

00:02:05.669 --> 00:02:07.772
each link passes its change on to the

00:02:07.833 --> 00:02:09.756
next, multiplied by its own rate.

00:02:10.538 --> 00:02:12.344
Rates along a chain multiply:

00:02:12.908 --> 00:02:14.955
d y by d u, times d u

00:02:15.016 --> 00:02:15.638
by d x.

00:02:16.308 --> 00:02:18.476
Now plug in the outsides from this unit.

00:02:19.119 --> 00:02:20.924
For e to the power of an inside

00:02:20.965 --> 00:02:23.211
part, copy e to that power,

00:02:23.714 --> 00:02:25.960
then multiply by the power's derivative.

00:02:26.703 --> 00:02:28.725
For the natural log of an inside part,

00:02:29.147 --> 00:02:31.770
the derivative is the inside's derivative, over the

00:02:31.891 --> 00:02:32.751
inside itself,

00:02:33.393 --> 00:02:34.795
and the inside has to be positive.

00:02:35.618 --> 00:02:38.347
For sine of an inside part, it's cos

00:02:38.428 --> 00:02:41.138
of the same inside, times the inside's derivative.

00:02:41.821 --> 00:02:43.824
And for cos, it's minus sine of the

00:02:43.845 --> 00:02:46.310
same inside, times the inside's derivative.

00:02:46.993 --> 00:02:49.380
Each time, the inside stays unchanged.

00:02:50.225 --> 00:02:52.332
For instance, e to the x squared has

00:02:52.353 --> 00:02:54.762
derivative two x, times e to the x

00:02:54.783 --> 00:02:55.164
squared.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:56.539
First example.

00:02:57.128 --> 00:03:00.116
Differentiate y equals e to the sine x.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.565
The outside is e to a power, and

00:03:03.606 --> 00:03:04.487
the inside is sine x.

00:03:06.012 --> 00:03:08.716
Copy e to the sine x, then multiply

00:03:08.817 --> 00:03:11.080
by the derivative of sine x, which is

00:03:11.222 --> 00:03:11.662
cos x.

00:03:12.624 --> 00:03:14.708
So d y by d x is e

00:03:14.749 --> 00:03:16.933
to the sine x, times cos x.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.664
Now look at the graph at pi over

00:03:19.705 --> 00:03:19.905
two.

00:03:20.608 --> 00:03:22.833
Cos of pi over two is zero, so

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:23.896
the gradient is zero.

00:03:24.619 --> 00:03:26.983
The inside, sine x, is at its peak

00:03:27.164 --> 00:03:29.448
and stops changing, so the whole curve goes

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:29.989
flat too.

00:03:31.055 --> 00:03:32.687
Swap the order, and the answer changes.

00:03:33.353 --> 00:03:35.596
For sine of e to the x, the

00:03:35.657 --> 00:03:38.561
outside is sine, so the derivative is cos

00:03:38.763 --> 00:03:40.745
of e to the x, times e to

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:41.106
the x.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:45.397
Second example: y equals the natural log of

00:03:45.517 --> 00:03:46.301
cos x.

00:03:47.143 --> 00:03:49.147
A log needs a positive input, so this

00:03:49.187 --> 00:03:51.771
curve only exists where cos x is positive,

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.736
for example between minus pi over two and

00:03:54.776 --> 00:03:55.397
pi over two.

00:03:56.238 --> 00:03:58.001
The outside is the natural log,

00:03:58.503 --> 00:04:01.389
so the derivative is the inside's derivative, over

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:01.930
the inside.

00:04:02.493 --> 00:04:05.438
That's minus sine x, over cos x, which

00:04:05.499 --> 00:04:06.661
is minus tan x,

00:04:07.263 --> 00:04:08.966
but only where cos x is positive.

00:04:09.828 --> 00:04:11.672
At pi over four, it's minus one,

00:04:12.215 --> 00:04:14.098
and the tangent on the graph agrees.

00:04:14.975 --> 00:04:17.042
Third example, with cos on the outside.

00:04:17.565 --> 00:04:20.915
Differentiate y equals cos of, x squared plus

00:04:21.057 --> 00:04:21.196
one.

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:24.022
The outside is cos, so its slope is

00:04:24.123 --> 00:04:27.288
minus sine of the same inside: minus sine

00:04:27.409 --> 00:04:28.630
of, x squared plus one.

00:04:29.474 --> 00:04:31.940
The inside's derivative is two x, because the

00:04:32.061 --> 00:04:32.903
one is a constant.

00:04:33.726 --> 00:04:35.528
Multiply them, and d y by d x

00:04:35.729 --> 00:04:38.614
is minus two x, sine of, x squared

00:04:38.675 --> 00:04:39.135
plus one.

00:04:40.018 --> 00:04:42.523
At x equals one, that's minus two sine

00:04:42.564 --> 00:04:42.784
two,

00:04:43.306 --> 00:04:45.009
about minus one point eight two.

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:48.001
Two things to keep: the minus sign from

00:04:48.022 --> 00:04:50.210
the outside, and the two x from the

00:04:50.311 --> 00:04:50.712
inside.

00:04:51.275 --> 00:04:52.663
Here's a short way to say the whole

00:04:52.744 --> 00:04:52.985
rule.

00:04:53.648 --> 00:04:56.697
Outside slope at the inside, times the inside

00:04:56.758 --> 00:04:57.038
slope.

00:04:57.603 --> 00:04:59.619
The words "at the inside" matter.

00:05:00.242 --> 00:05:02.906
For sine of x squared, the outside slope

00:05:02.988 --> 00:05:05.151
is cos of x squared, not cos x,

00:05:05.573 --> 00:05:07.336
and the inside slope is two x.

00:05:07.919 --> 00:05:10.133
So the derivative is two x cos of

00:05:10.154 --> 00:05:10.697
x squared.

00:05:11.441 --> 00:05:13.726
For the natural log, keep the inside positive,

00:05:14.028 --> 00:05:15.751
and use one over it for the outside

00:05:15.792 --> 00:05:16.052
slope.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:19.228
Your turn.

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:22.828
Differentiate y equals the natural log of, x

00:05:22.869 --> 00:05:23.933
squared minus nine.

00:05:24.516 --> 00:05:26.303
Then state the values of x for which

00:05:26.344 --> 00:05:27.327
your answer is valid.

00:05:27.932 --> 00:05:28.764
Pause here to answer.

00:05:39.655 --> 00:05:42.462
The inside is x squared minus nine, with

00:05:42.483 --> 00:05:43.505
derivative two x.

00:05:44.129 --> 00:05:46.299
So d y by d x is two

00:05:46.441 --> 00:05:48.250
x, over x squared minus nine.

00:05:49.152 --> 00:05:51.175
The log needs x squared minus nine to

00:05:51.216 --> 00:05:53.639
be positive, so x squared is more than

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:53.980
nine:

00:05:54.762 --> 00:05:56.864
x is less than minus three, or more

00:05:56.906 --> 00:05:57.345
than three.

00:05:58.028 --> 00:06:00.394
Saying only x isn't plus or minus three

00:06:00.797 --> 00:06:01.337
isn't enough.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.306
Between minus three and three, the inside is

00:06:04.427 --> 00:06:06.252
negative, and the log doesn't exist.

00:06:08.003 --> 00:06:08.386
Last one.

00:06:09.091 --> 00:06:11.959
For y equals sine of the natural log

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.945
of x, with x positive,

00:06:14.486 --> 00:06:15.930
find d y by d x.

00:06:16.573 --> 00:06:19.203
Then find the exact gradient at x equals

00:06:19.364 --> 00:06:19.484
e.

00:06:20.148 --> 00:06:20.912
Pause here to answer.

00:06:32.561 --> 00:06:35.176
The outside is sine, and the inside is

00:06:35.216 --> 00:06:36.202
the natural log of x.

00:06:36.744 --> 00:06:39.049
So d y by d x is cos

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.394
of the natural log of x, times one

00:06:41.555 --> 00:06:42.016
over x.

00:06:42.917 --> 00:06:45.039
At x equals e, the natural log of

00:06:45.059 --> 00:06:48.042
e is one, so the gradient is cos

00:06:48.262 --> 00:06:50.624
one, over e, about point two.

00:06:51.366 --> 00:06:52.848
If you left out the one over x,

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:55.735
you'd get cos one, about point five four,

00:06:56.116 --> 00:06:57.839
and you'd have skipped the inside slope.

00:06:59.374 --> 00:07:01.295
So for any of these functions with an

00:07:01.336 --> 00:07:04.398
inside part, take the outside's slope at the

00:07:04.459 --> 00:07:04.878
inside,

00:07:05.399 --> 00:07:07.781
and multiply by the inside's slope.

00:07:08.544 --> 00:07:10.533
And for a log, keep the inside positive.

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:11.656
Next,

00:07:12.259 --> 00:07:15.465
two functions multiplied together, like e to the

00:07:15.607 --> 00:07:16.768
x times sine x.

00:07:17.814 --> 00:07:19.650
How do both parts set the slope?

00:07:22.321 --> 00:07:23.205
Here are the key notes.

00:07:23.727 --> 00:07:25.496
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:25.516 --> 00:07:25.998
to copy them.
